  "notes": [
    "Every parameter Pxxxx is the holding register of the same number (P0900 is register 900); the Modicon address is 40001 + the number. Values are integers without decimal point.",
    "Address 1 to 247 and speed come from the DIP switch S2 (address 1 to 127; speeds 9600 to 76800 bit/s, no parity with 2 stop bits or even parity with 1 stop bit) or, with register 625 = 1, from registers 626 and 627. The switch also sets the CANopen address. A change takes effect after power-up. Functions 01, 02, 03, 04, 05, 06, 15, 16, 22, 23 and 43 are available.",
    "Parameters are not retentive by default: write 1 to register 204 to save them to flash.",
    "Only the head unit and the digital I/O accessory of slot 1 are listed. The accessories of slots 2 to 8 repeat the slot 1 parameters at +100 per slot (P1200 for slot 2, up to P1800); the analog input, analog output, strain gauge and SCW starter accessories (parameters P3000 and up, P5000 and up, P7000 and up, P9000 and up) are not mapped here.",
    "The manual does not say which word comes first in a 32-bit parameter. This map assumes the low word first, as the PLC300 manual does for the SoftPLC; check it against the DIs of a real unit.",
    "Written from the manufacturer's manual; not tested on a device."
  ],
